 "remarks": "Exceptional Downtown Greenwich townhouse living in a coveted location nestled between Bruce Park and the Bruce Museum. This sun-filled 3-bedroom, 2.5-bath residence offers an inviting combination of space, privacy and convenience, just moments from Greenwich Avenue, the train station and Greenwich Harbor. The gracious open floor plan is designed for both comfortable everyday living and entertaining, with spacious living and dining areas anchored by a handsome wood-burning fieldstone fireplace. The well-appointed kitchen features abundant storage, stone countertops, custom pantry and stainless-steel appliances, and opens seamlessly to the main living spaces. French doors lead to a private, beautifully landscaped stone terrace, surrounded by lush greenery and mature evergreen screening. Custom built-ins and powder room complete the main level. Upstairs, the generous primary suite is joined by a second bedroom and full bath, along with brand new washer/dryer. The top floor offers a versatile 3rd bedroom or office, highlighted by a skylight and oversized walk-in storage, providing exceptional flexibility for guests, home office or additional living space. Set within a well-maintained 12-unit townhouse community, the residence includes central heat/AC, two assigned parking spaces, separate bike storage and offers the rare ease of a true walk-to-everything Downtown Greenwich lifestyle, with shopping, dining, parks, the harbor and Metro-North all close at hand.",
